In C, [38;5;10matoi("-5")[0m returns [38;5;10m-5[0m as an [38;5;10mint[0m, which is printed with [38;5;10m%d[0m (showing [38;5;10m-5[0m). It's then implicitly cast to [38;5;10msize_t[0m (unsigned) when passed to [38;5;10mstrncmp[0m. Similarly, [38;5;10matoi("999999999999999")[0m overflows [38;5;10mint[0m and wraps to [38;5;10m-1530494977[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation immediately cast [38;5;10mc_atoi()[0m to [38;5;10musize[0m, so the printed value was the unsigned interpretation (e.g., [38;5;10m18446744073709551611[0m instead of [38;5;10m-5[0m).[0m[0m
